  "id": "unipolar-disorder",
  "term": "unipolar disorder",
  "definition": "In this source, unipolar disorder refers to a condition marked by depressive symptoms that can be mistaken for bipolar disorder in clinical practice. It is described as being associated with cognitive deficits, including poorer working memory, and these difficulties may still be present even when symptoms are remitted.",
